# Neo Voice to MIDI parameters (docs/specs/voice-to-midi.md). The order changes only with a version (machines.md §3.2): songs and presets
# store values by position. Regenerate: python3 tools/gen-machine-params.py Machines/NeoVoiceToMidi
namespace NeoBuzz.VoiceToMidi
class NeoVoiceToMidiMachine
summary Turns a voice into MIDI and lets it pass through (monitor blend 0 to 100 %). Pitch: the sung note, locked to a key or scale, with stickiness, octave shift, pitch bend (free or anchored), dynamic or fixed velocity, minimum note length and legato. Triggers: up to 8 sounds you train in one pass (voice percussion or any short sound) play notes at once with the pitch. Chords: diatonic chords that follow the sung root, with suggestions that fit the melody. Expression: the voice level and the vowels aa, oo and ee as MIDI controllers, each with thresholds, range and channel. The MIDI goes to a target machine, to an external MIDI device, and is a MIDI From source for armed tracks. Use it to play synths and drums with your voice, or to sing a melody into a clip.

group Input
Monitor "Monitor" 0 100 100 pct 0 | Dry voice at the output: 0 is silent, 100 % is the input as it came
    how Sets how much of the dry voice reaches the output, from 0% (silent) to 100% (as it came in).
    sound At 0% you hear only what the synth plays from the MIDI; a little dry voice makes a guide to sing against.
Range "Range" 0 1 1 enum Low_latency Quality | Voice range: Low latency (about 8 ms, from 100 Hz) or Quality (about 18 ms, from 70 Hz)
    how Chooses the pitch analysis: Low latency (about 8 ms, from 100 Hz) or Quality (about 18 ms, from 70 Hz).
    sound Low latency answers sooner but can wobble on low voices; Quality is steadier and reaches lower notes.
Level "Level" 0 50 20 lin -70 -20 dB 0 | The quietest voice that plays a note: under this level the pitch is not read
    how Sets the quietest voice level, from -70 to -20 dB, that plays a note.
    sound Raising it ignores room noise and breath; set too high it misses soft singing.
group Pitch
Pitch "Pitch" 0 1 1 switch | The sung pitch plays notes
    how Switches the sung pitch playing notes on or off.
    sound Off leaves the triggers, the chords and the controllers running without single notes.
Lock "Lock" 0 3 0 enum Off Set_key Song_key Suggest | Off: every semitone. Set key: the Root and Scale. Song key: the key of the song (the song's Key entry), else Root and Scale. Suggest: the key found from the notes you sang so far
    how Chooses how notes are kept to a key: Off, the Root and Scale, the song's key or a key found from what you sang.
    sound Locked notes land on the key whatever the voice does; Off follows every semitone you sing.
Root "Root" 0 11 0 enum C "C#" D "D#" E F "F#" G "G#" A "A#" B | The key's root note
    how Sets the key's root note from C to B.
    sound It moves every in-key note with it; the scale keyboard shows the result.
Scale "Scale" 0 13 0 enum Major Minor Dorian Phrygian Lydian Mixolydian Locrian Harmonic_minor Melodic_minor Major_pentatonic Minor_pentatonic Blues Whole_tone Custom | The scale the voice is locked to
    how Chooses the scale of the key from 14 choices, including a Custom set of notes.
    sound Major sounds bright, minor darker, pentatonic and blues leave out the notes that clash.
Custom "Custom notes" 0 4095 2741 int 0 | The notes of the Custom scale, one bit per note from C (bit 0) to B (bit 11)
    how Holds the Custom scale's twelve notes, one bit each from C to B.
    sound Only the notes you switch on in the keyboard can play when Scale is Custom.
Muted "Muted notes" 0 4095 0 int 0 | Notes never played, one bit per note from C to B: the voice goes to the nearest note that is on
    how Holds the notes that never play, one bit each from C to B (click a key on the keyboard).
    sound A muted note is replaced by the nearest note that is on, so the melody avoids it.
Octave "Octave" 0 6 3 int -3 oct signed | Octave shift of the pitch notes
    how Shifts the pitch notes by whole octaves, from -3 to +3.
    sound The same tune plays higher or lower on the synth without singing in another register.
Stick "Stickiness" 0 100 25 lin 0 100 cents 0 | How far past the middle between two notes the voice must go before the note changes (a hysteresis)
    how Sets how far past the middle between two notes the voice must go before the note changes, from 0 to 100 cents.
    sound More stickiness holds a wobbly note steady; none follows every small move.
Settle "Settle" 0 200 30 lin 0 200 ms 0 | How long a new note must be held before it plays or replaces the one sounding
    how Sets how long a new note must be held before it plays or replaces the one sounding, from 0 to 200 ms.
    sound Longer settling removes grace notes and slides at the cost of a later note start.
Bend "Pitch bend" 0 12 0 enum Off "±1 st" "±2 st" "±3 st" "±4 st" "±5 st" "±6 st" "±7 st" "±8 st" "±9 st" "±10 st" "±11 st" "±12 st" | Pitch bend range: the voice's distance from the note is sent as bend. Set the same range on the synth
    how Sets the pitch bend range from off to plus or minus 12 semitones.
    sound The voice's distance from its note moves the synth's pitch by this much; set the synth to the same range.
BendMode "Bend mode" 0 1 0 enum Free Anchored | Free: bend follows every wobble. Anchored: the note stays put until the voice moves farther than the Anchor from its middle, then it bends
    how Chooses Free bend or Anchored bend.
    sound Free follows every wobble; Anchored keeps the note still until the voice leaves it, then bends.
Anchor "Anchor" 5 100 35 lin 5 100 cents 0 | Anchored bend: how far from the note's middle the voice must move before the bend starts
    how Sets how far from the note's middle the voice must move, from 5 to 100 cents, before the bend starts.
    sound A larger anchor keeps vibrato from bending the note; a small one bends at once.
VelMode "Velocity" 0 1 0 enum Dynamic Fixed | Dynamic: from how loud you sing the note. Fixed: always the Fixed velocity
    how Chooses note velocity from the voice (Dynamic) or always the Fixed velocity.
    sound Dynamic plays soft singing softly; Fixed gives every note the same strength.
Fixed "Fixed velocity" 1 127 100 int 0 | The velocity of every note in Fixed mode, and the loudest in Dynamic
    how Sets the fixed velocity, and the loudest in Dynamic, from 1 to 127.
    sound Higher values play louder or brighter on most synths.
VelMin "Softest velocity" 1 127 25 int 0 | Dynamic: the velocity of the softest note
    how Sets the velocity of the softest note in Dynamic mode, from 1 to 127.
    sound A higher minimum keeps soft notes audible.
Soft "Soft level" 0 50 20 lin -70 -20 dB 0 | Dynamic: the voice level that gives the softest velocity
    how Sets the voice level, from -70 to -20 dB, that gives the softest velocity.
    sound Raise it if quiet singing plays too loud a note.
Loud "Loud level" 0 40 28 lin -40 0 dB 0 | Dynamic: the voice level that gives the loudest velocity
    how Sets the voice level, from -40 to 0 dB, that gives the loudest velocity.
    sound Lower it so ordinary singing reaches full velocity.
MinNote "Min note length" 0 100 12 lin 0 500 ms 0 | A note lasts at least this long, however short the voice was
    how Sets the shortest a note lasts, from 0 to 100 ms mapped to 0 to 500 ms.
    sound Short sung notes still last long enough for the synth to sound.
Legato "Legato" 0 1 0 switch | A new note starts before the old one stops (for mono synths with legato), instead of after
    how Starts a new note before the old one stops when switched on.
    sound Mono synths then glide between notes instead of retriggering.
PitchCh "Pitch channel" 0 15 0 int 1 | MIDI channel of the pitch notes
    how Sets the MIDI channel of the pitch notes, from 1 to 16.
    sound It selects which synth or part plays the sung line.
group Triggers
Triggers "Triggers" 0 1 1 switch | Trained sounds play notes
    how Switches the trained sounds playing notes on or off.
    sound Off leaves only the pitch part.
Window "Window" 0 1 1 enum Fast Accurate | The slice of each hit the classifier hears: Fast 18 ms (about 15 ms after the hit) or Accurate 30 ms (about 27 ms, a few points more right)
    how Chooses the slice of each hit the classifier hears: Fast (18 ms) or Accurate (30 ms).
    sound Accurate names sounds a few points more reliably and plays about 12 ms later.
Sensitivity "Sensitivity" 0 100 67 pct 0 | How soft a hit may be and still count (the onset threshold)
    how Sets how soft a hit may be and still count, from 0 to 100%.
    sound Higher values catch quiet hits and risk catching breaths and clicks.
Gap "Min gap" 0 240 50 lin 60 300 ms 0 | The shortest time between two hits. 100 to 120 ms suits a voice (the vowel after a consonant is not a second hit)
    how Sets the shortest time between two hits, from 60 to 300 ms.
    sound About 110 ms stops the vowel after a consonant counting as a second hit.
Overlap "Overlap" 0 1 0 enum Triggers_win Both | Triggers win: a sound taken for a trigger does not also play a pitch note. Both: the voice also plays its pitch
    how Chooses whether a sound taken for a trigger also plays a pitch note: Triggers win or Both.
    sound Triggers win keeps a kick from also playing a low note; Both lets the voice play its pitch too.
Length "Trigger length" 0 490 50 lin 10 500 ms 0 | How long each trigger note is held before its note off
    how Sets how long each trigger note is held, from 10 to 500 ms.
    sound Short notes suit drums that ring by themselves; long ones suit sustained sounds.
TrigCh "Trigger channel" 0 15 9 int 1 | MIDI channel of the trigger notes (10 is the drum channel)
    how Sets the MIDI channel of the trigger notes, from 1 to 16.
    sound Channel 10 is the drum channel of most drum machines.
T1Note "Sound 1 note" 0 127 36 int 0 | MIDI note of sound 1 (Kick by default)
    how Sets the MIDI note sound 1 plays, from 0 to 127.
    sound Choose the drum or note you want that sound to play; defaults follow the usual drum map.
T1Vel "Sound 1 velocity" 0 127 0 int 0 | 0: from how hard the hit was. 1 to 127: always this velocity
    how Sets sound 1's velocity from 1 to 127, or 0 to take it from how hard the hit was.
    sound Zero makes harder hits play louder; a number makes every hit the same.
T1Sens "Sound 1 sensitivity" 0 100 50 pct 0 | How sure the classifier must be for sound 1: higher plays more of the doubtful hits
    how Sets how sure the classifier must be to play sound 1, from 0 to 100%.
    sound Higher values play it more readily but let other sounds through as it; lower ones play only clear hits.
T2Note "Sound 2 note" 0 127 38 int 0 | MIDI note of sound 2 (Snare by default)
    how Sets the MIDI note sound 2 plays, from 0 to 127.
    sound Choose the drum or note you want that sound to play; defaults follow the usual drum map.
T2Vel "Sound 2 velocity" 0 127 0 int 0 | 0: from how hard the hit was. 1 to 127: always this velocity
    how Sets sound 2's velocity from 1 to 127, or 0 to take it from how hard the hit was.
    sound Zero makes harder hits play louder; a number makes every hit the same.
T2Sens "Sound 2 sensitivity" 0 100 50 pct 0 | How sure the classifier must be for sound 2: higher plays more of the doubtful hits
    how Sets how sure the classifier must be to play sound 2, from 0 to 100%.
    sound Higher values play it more readily but let other sounds through as it; lower ones play only clear hits.
T3Note "Sound 3 note" 0 127 42 int 0 | MIDI note of sound 3 (Closed hat by default)
    how Sets the MIDI note sound 3 plays, from 0 to 127.
    sound Choose the drum or note you want that sound to play; defaults follow the usual drum map.
T3Vel "Sound 3 velocity" 0 127 0 int 0 | 0: from how hard the hit was. 1 to 127: always this velocity
    how Sets sound 3's velocity from 1 to 127, or 0 to take it from how hard the hit was.
    sound Zero makes harder hits play louder; a number makes every hit the same.
T3Sens "Sound 3 sensitivity" 0 100 50 pct 0 | How sure the classifier must be for sound 3: higher plays more of the doubtful hits
    how Sets how sure the classifier must be to play sound 3, from 0 to 100%.
    sound Higher values play it more readily but let other sounds through as it; lower ones play only clear hits.
T4Note "Sound 4 note" 0 127 46 int 0 | MIDI note of sound 4 (Open hat by default)
    how Sets the MIDI note sound 4 plays, from 0 to 127.
    sound Choose the drum or note you want that sound to play; defaults follow the usual drum map.
T4Vel "Sound 4 velocity" 0 127 0 int 0 | 0: from how hard the hit was. 1 to 127: always this velocity
    how Sets sound 4's velocity from 1 to 127, or 0 to take it from how hard the hit was.
    sound Zero makes harder hits play louder; a number makes every hit the same.
T4Sens "Sound 4 sensitivity" 0 100 50 pct 0 | How sure the classifier must be for sound 4: higher plays more of the doubtful hits
    how Sets how sure the classifier must be to play sound 4, from 0 to 100%.
    sound Higher values play it more readily but let other sounds through as it; lower ones play only clear hits.
T5Note "Sound 5 note" 0 127 39 int 0 | MIDI note of sound 5 (Clap by default)
    how Sets the MIDI note sound 5 plays, from 0 to 127.
    sound Choose the drum or note you want that sound to play; defaults follow the usual drum map.
T5Vel "Sound 5 velocity" 0 127 0 int 0 | 0: from how hard the hit was. 1 to 127: always this velocity
    how Sets sound 5's velocity from 1 to 127, or 0 to take it from how hard the hit was.
    sound Zero makes harder hits play louder; a number makes every hit the same.
T5Sens "Sound 5 sensitivity" 0 100 50 pct 0 | How sure the classifier must be for sound 5: higher plays more of the doubtful hits
    how Sets how sure the classifier must be to play sound 5, from 0 to 100%.
    sound Higher values play it more readily but let other sounds through as it; lower ones play only clear hits.
T6Note "Sound 6 note" 0 127 37 int 0 | MIDI note of sound 6 (Rim by default)
    how Sets the MIDI note sound 6 plays, from 0 to 127.
    sound Choose the drum or note you want that sound to play; defaults follow the usual drum map.
T6Vel "Sound 6 velocity" 0 127 0 int 0 | 0: from how hard the hit was. 1 to 127: always this velocity
    how Sets sound 6's velocity from 1 to 127, or 0 to take it from how hard the hit was.
    sound Zero makes harder hits play louder; a number makes every hit the same.
T6Sens "Sound 6 sensitivity" 0 100 50 pct 0 | How sure the classifier must be for sound 6: higher plays more of the doubtful hits
    how Sets how sure the classifier must be to play sound 6, from 0 to 100%.
    sound Higher values play it more readily but let other sounds through as it; lower ones play only clear hits.
T7Note "Sound 7 note" 0 127 49 int 0 | MIDI note of sound 7 (Crash by default)
    how Sets the MIDI note sound 7 plays, from 0 to 127.
    sound Choose the drum or note you want that sound to play; defaults follow the usual drum map.
T7Vel "Sound 7 velocity" 0 127 0 int 0 | 0: from how hard the hit was. 1 to 127: always this velocity
    how Sets sound 7's velocity from 1 to 127, or 0 to take it from how hard the hit was.
    sound Zero makes harder hits play louder; a number makes every hit the same.
T7Sens "Sound 7 sensitivity" 0 100 50 pct 0 | How sure the classifier must be for sound 7: higher plays more of the doubtful hits
    how Sets how sure the classifier must be to play sound 7, from 0 to 100%.
    sound Higher values play it more readily but let other sounds through as it; lower ones play only clear hits.
T8Note "Sound 8 note" 0 127 51 int 0 | MIDI note of sound 8 (Ride by default)
    how Sets the MIDI note sound 8 plays, from 0 to 127.
    sound Choose the drum or note you want that sound to play; defaults follow the usual drum map.
T8Vel "Sound 8 velocity" 0 127 0 int 0 | 0: from how hard the hit was. 1 to 127: always this velocity
    how Sets sound 8's velocity from 1 to 127, or 0 to take it from how hard the hit was.
    sound Zero makes harder hits play louder; a number makes every hit the same.
T8Sens "Sound 8 sensitivity" 0 100 50 pct 0 | How sure the classifier must be for sound 8: higher plays more of the doubtful hits
    how Sets how sure the classifier must be to play sound 8, from 0 to 100%.
    sound Higher values play it more readily but let other sounds through as it; lower ones play only clear hits.
group Chords
Chords "Chords" 0 1 0 switch | The pitch also plays a chord on its own channel
    how Switches the chords on or off.
    sound On, every sung note also plays a chord of the key on its own channel.
ChordFollow "Chord follows" 0 1 0 enum Root Melody | Root: the sung note is the chord's root (diatonic to the key). Melody: the chord of the key that fits the sung note
    how Chooses whether the sung note is the chord's root or the chord that fits the sung note is played.
    sound Root builds on the note you sing; Melody picks the chord of the key that contains it.
ChordType "Chord type" 0 1 0 enum Triads Sevenths | Three or four notes
    how Chooses triads (three notes) or sevenths (four notes).
    sound Sevenths sound jazzier and richer; triads are plain and strong.
Inversion "Inversion" 0 3 3 enum Root First Second Auto | Auto keeps the chords close to each other (smooth voice leading)
    how Chooses the chord's inversion: Root, First, Second or Auto.
    sound Auto keeps successive chords close together for smooth movement.
Spread "Voicing" 0 2 0 enum Close Open Wide | Close: all within an octave. Open: the second note from the top an octave down. Wide: the root doubled an octave down
    how Chooses how the chord notes are spread: Close, Open or Wide.
    sound Close is tight and thick; Wide is airy and spread over more than an octave.
ChordOct "Chord octave" 0 4 2 int -2 oct signed | Register of the chords (0 is the octave of middle C minus one)
    how Sets the register of the chords, from -2 to +2 octaves.
    sound Lower registers make a pad under the voice; higher ones make a shimmer above.
ChordCh "Chord channel" 0 15 1 int 1 | MIDI channel of the chords
    how Sets the MIDI channel of the chords, from 1 to 16.
    sound It selects which synth or part plays the chords.
ChordVel "Chord velocity" 0 100 80 pct 0 | The chords' velocity as a share of the pitch note's
    how Sets the chords' velocity as a share of the note's velocity, from 0 to 100%.
    sound Lower values keep the chords behind the melody.
group Expression
LvlOn "Level on" 0 1 0 switch | Level plays a controller
    how Switches the voice level playing a MIDI controller on or off.
    sound On, the voice level moves the controller's target, such as a filter or volume.
LvlCC "Level controller" 0 126 10 int 1 | The controller number of Level
    how Sets the controller number for the voice level, from 1 to 127.
    sound Pick the number the synth's target is mapped to (74 is often the filter cutoff).
LvlMin "Level min" 0 100 0 pct 0 | Level at or under this gives the low end of the range (share of -60 to 0 dB)
    how Sets the amount of the voice level, from 0 to 100%, that gives the low end of the range.
    sound Raising it makes the controller reach its low value sooner.
LvlMax "Level max" 0 100 100 pct 0 | Level at or over this gives the high end of the range (share of -60 to 0 dB)
    how Sets the amount of the voice level, from 0 to 100%, that gives the high end of the range.
    sound Lowering it makes the controller reach its high value sooner.
LvlLo "Level low value" 0 127 0 int 0 | The controller value at the min
    how Sets the controller value sent at the low end of the voice level, from 0 to 127.
    sound Swap it with the high value to turn the control upside down.
LvlHi "Level high value" 0 127 127 int 0 | The controller value at the max
    how Sets the controller value sent at the high end of the voice level, from 0 to 127.
    sound Lower it to limit how far the control moves its target.
LvlCh "Level channel" 0 15 0 int 1 | MIDI channel of Level
    how Sets the MIDI channel of the controller for the voice level, from 1 to 16.
    sound It selects which synth or part the control moves.
AaOn "Vowel aa on" 0 1 0 switch | Vowel aa plays a controller
    how Switches the vowel aa playing a MIDI controller on or off.
    sound On, the vowel aa moves the controller's target, such as a filter or volume.
AaCC "Vowel aa controller" 0 126 73 int 1 | The controller number of Vowel aa
    how Sets the controller number for the vowel aa, from 1 to 127.
    sound Pick the number the synth's target is mapped to (74 is often the filter cutoff).
AaMin "Vowel aa min" 0 100 0 pct 0 | Vowel aa at or under this gives the low end of the range
    how Sets the amount of the vowel aa, from 0 to 100%, that gives the low end of the range.
    sound Raising it makes the controller reach its low value sooner.
AaMax "Vowel aa max" 0 100 100 pct 0 | Vowel aa at or over this gives the high end of the range
    how Sets the amount of the vowel aa, from 0 to 100%, that gives the high end of the range.
    sound Lowering it makes the controller reach its high value sooner.
AaLo "Vowel aa low value" 0 127 0 int 0 | The controller value at the min
    how Sets the controller value sent at the low end of the vowel aa, from 0 to 127.
    sound Swap it with the high value to turn the control upside down.
AaHi "Vowel aa high value" 0 127 127 int 0 | The controller value at the max
    how Sets the controller value sent at the high end of the vowel aa, from 0 to 127.
    sound Lower it to limit how far the control moves its target.
AaCh "Vowel aa channel" 0 15 0 int 1 | MIDI channel of Vowel aa
    how Sets the MIDI channel of the controller for the vowel aa, from 1 to 16.
    sound It selects which synth or part the control moves.
OoOn "Vowel oo on" 0 1 0 switch | Vowel oo plays a controller
    how Switches the vowel oo playing a MIDI controller on or off.
    sound On, the vowel oo moves the controller's target, such as a filter or volume.
OoCC "Vowel oo controller" 0 126 70 int 1 | The controller number of Vowel oo
    how Sets the controller number for the vowel oo, from 1 to 127.
    sound Pick the number the synth's target is mapped to (74 is often the filter cutoff).
OoMin "Vowel oo min" 0 100 0 pct 0 | Vowel oo at or under this gives the low end of the range
    how Sets the amount of the vowel oo, from 0 to 100%, that gives the low end of the range.
    sound Raising it makes the controller reach its low value sooner.
OoMax "Vowel oo max" 0 100 100 pct 0 | Vowel oo at or over this gives the high end of the range
    how Sets the amount of the vowel oo, from 0 to 100%, that gives the high end of the range.
    sound Lowering it makes the controller reach its high value sooner.
OoLo "Vowel oo low value" 0 127 0 int 0 | The controller value at the min
    how Sets the controller value sent at the low end of the vowel oo, from 0 to 127.
    sound Swap it with the high value to turn the control upside down.
OoHi "Vowel oo high value" 0 127 127 int 0 | The controller value at the max
    how Sets the controller value sent at the high end of the vowel oo, from 0 to 127.
    sound Lower it to limit how far the control moves its target.
OoCh "Vowel oo channel" 0 15 0 int 1 | MIDI channel of Vowel oo
    how Sets the MIDI channel of the controller for the vowel oo, from 1 to 16.
    sound It selects which synth or part the control moves.
EeOn "Vowel ee on" 0 1 0 switch | Vowel ee plays a controller
    how Switches the vowel ee playing a MIDI controller on or off.
    sound On, the vowel ee moves the controller's target, such as a filter or volume.
EeCC "Vowel ee controller" 0 126 0 int 1 | The controller number of Vowel ee
    how Sets the controller number for the vowel ee, from 1 to 127.
    sound Pick the number the synth's target is mapped to (74 is often the filter cutoff).
EeMin "Vowel ee min" 0 100 0 pct 0 | Vowel ee at or under this gives the low end of the range
    how Sets the amount of the vowel ee, from 0 to 100%, that gives the low end of the range.
    sound Raising it makes the controller reach its low value sooner.
EeMax "Vowel ee max" 0 100 100 pct 0 | Vowel ee at or over this gives the high end of the range
    how Sets the amount of the vowel ee, from 0 to 100%, that gives the high end of the range.
    sound Lowering it makes the controller reach its high value sooner.
EeLo "Vowel ee low value" 0 127 0 int 0 | The controller value at the min
    how Sets the controller value sent at the low end of the vowel ee, from 0 to 127.
    sound Swap it with the high value to turn the control upside down.
EeHi "Vowel ee high value" 0 127 127 int 0 | The controller value at the max
    how Sets the controller value sent at the high end of the vowel ee, from 0 to 127.
    sound Lower it to limit how far the control moves its target.
EeCh "Vowel ee channel" 0 15 0 int 1 | MIDI channel of Vowel ee
    how Sets the MIDI channel of the controller for the vowel ee, from 1 to 16.
    sound It selects which synth or part the control moves.

# What the machine measures (NeoVoiceToMidiMachine.Readings, machine_readings).
reading note number | The pitch note sounding now (MIDI number), 0 when none
reading sung_midi number | The pitch the voice is singing, in fractional MIDI notes (0 when unvoiced)
reading voiced flag | 1 while the voice is voiced
reading key_root number | The key in use: its root, 0 (C) to 11 (B), -1 for none
reading key_minor flag | 1 when the key in use is minor
reading level_db dB | The voice level, dBFS
reading vowel_aa number | The vowel weights, 0 to 1
reading vowel_oo number | The vowel weight oo, 0 to 1
reading vowel_ee number | The vowel weight ee, 0 to 1
reading last_trigger number | The last sound that played (1 to 8), 0 when none yet
reading trained_sounds number | How many sounds have training examples
reading note_latency_ms ms | How long after the voice starts a note plays: the pitch window plus Settle
